Package: linuxeasyhotspot
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: MazMorrDev <marconchelo12@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: @SHLIBS@, network-manager (>= 1.30), iproute2, polkitd | policykit-1, dbus
Recommends: pkexec
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/OWNER/LinuxEasyHotspot
Description: Share your internet over Wi-Fi in one click
 Linux Easy Hotspot creates a Wi-Fi hotspot through NetworkManager with as
 few steps as possible: network name, password and a QR code to join.
 .
 It supports Router (NAT), Bridge and Local-only modes, choosing the
 Wi-Fi adapter, band, channel and internet source, and shows the
 connected and remembered devices, with the hotspot's total and current
 data usage. USB Wi-Fi adapters are detected when plugged in.
 .
 Per-device speed limits, priority, approval of new devices and data
 caps are provided by the included leh-shaper helper, a small
 polkit-protected system D-Bus service started on demand.
